{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>I</b> — I reckon myself as poor and needy, and I cannot stand against my enemies." "<b>be thought of for me</b> — this and the reason is the lowliness of my heart. Or לי is in place of 'on my account,' as in: 'who fights for you.'" "<b>do not delay</b> — participle, as in: 'why did they delay.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:25.307006217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}